 # Engineering Review Log
 
+## 2026-09-22 — Model v26: rollout-labelled fitted policy iteration (NMCC-FPI)
+
+Design, evidence and run instructions: `docs/NMCC_FPI_V26_DESIGN_20260922.md`.
+Motivation: the four issues and the capacity finding in
+`docs/V25_PILOT_REVIEW_20260922.md`.
+
+### Design
+
+- New actor objective `nmccPiActorObjective = "fitted_value"`. Exact CRN branch
+  labels are full-horizon values of the fixed route-saving base policy
+  (`nmccPiBranchHorizon = 0`). They are stored permanently.
+- Every rollout, the whole GNN/LSTM network (value ensemble plus world-model
+  auxiliaries) is refit on the store, from scratch by default, with
+  validation early stopping.
+- The executed rule is the base policy until a safe-policy-improvement gate,
+  run on exhaustively branched holdout episodes, certifies
+  `prior + λ(μ − βσ)` for a given (model, λ, β).
+- Branch allocation: exhaustive at the first two decisions and at every
+  holdout decision; otherwise base, executed and greedy cells plus
+  optimistic and random support.
+- New torch-free module `FittedPolicyIteration.py`: label store, splits,
+  family scales, decision rule, gate, allocation, paired learning curve and
+  FPI convergence.
+- Decision interface, applied to every strategy:
+  - token-bucket schedule with catch-up (`shelterDecisionCatchUp`);
+  - optional operator-known scenario descriptors (`scenarioDescriptors`:
+    panic susceptibility, `P/(P+10⁴)`, `H/(H+3)`);
+  - new `route_saving` benchmark strategy, identical to the base policy.
+- Measurement:
+  - per-episode exact paired gains (`nmcc_fpi_episode_*`);
+  - gate diagnostics (`nmcc_fpi_gate_*`) and a JSONL gate log next to the
+    checkpoint;
+  - `backtest`/`multicity_backtest` audit FPI runs with `fpi_convergence`
+    instead of return stationarity and the PPO KL target;
+  - matched-interface verification reports realized-capacity parity.
+- Scenario generality:
+  - orthogonal-array curricula over pedestrians × hazards × panic
+    (`config/scenario_general_training_curriculum_nmcc_fpi_v26.json`, pilot
+    `config/state_college_training_curriculum_nmcc_fpi_v26_pilot.json`);
+  - multicity evaluation applies the curriculum learner contract to every
+    strategy and can cycle through curriculum scenarios.
+- `fpi_label_workers.py` runs parallel collect-only label workers against the
+  learner's checkpoint and store.
+
+### Reward check
+
+- No defect in `RewardProcessor`. `tests/test_reward_contract.py` pins the
+  outcome ordering, per-step = per-interval additivity and population-scale
+  invariance.
+- The cross-scenario issue is the value scale of a fixed-capacity shelter
+  (∝ capacity/P). The learner normalizes per family; the objective is
+  unchanged.
+
+### Compatibility
+
+- `MODEL_VERSION = 26`; the signature adds `decision_rule`, `token_rule`,
+  `fitted_policy_iteration` and `scenario_descriptors`.
+- Every new setting defaults to the v25 contract. The `GNN.prior_logits`
+  refactor is numerically identical. The v24 curriculum test skips v26-only
+  rows.
+- Behavior change in multicity evaluation: the curriculum learner contract is
+  now applied by default. `--evaluation-learner-contract none` restores the
+  old behavior.
+- The policy-cache fingerprint now includes the learner modules.
+
+### Verification
+
+- 107 torch-free tests across 12 modules pass, including 33 new ones.
+- `flake8 --select=F` is clean. `pyright` adds no errors over the v25
+  baseline except one numpy-stub false positive.
+- An independent static review of the torch integration found eight defects,
+  all fixed:
+  - no-gradient minibatch crash;
+  - σ polluted by unidentified member levels (now base-differenced);
+  - shared collector random streams;
+  - catch-up combined with hybrid-NMCC credit (now refused);
+  - device-memory replay cache (now CPU, with eviction);
+  - refit discarded when validation had no contrast;
+  - holdout exploration (now ε = 0);
+  - evaluation without the learner contract.
+- Gate operating characteristics on real 3-tape full-horizon labels (400
+  splits, `runs/nmcc_v26_fpi_gate_validation_20260922.json`):
+  - a no-skill model is certified in 0.5% of splits (α = 10%);
+  - noisy-oracle models are certified 23–66% of the time, and never when
+    their true gain was negative;
+  - the 8-episode ridge replica (ρ = 0.29) would harm in 60% of splits if
+    deployed ungated; the gate kept the base policy.
+- **Not verified here:** `tests/test_fitted_policy_iteration_torch.py` and
+  the full suite need the `rlevacuation` environment. Torch is not
+  installable from this tool.
