+    """Is a deployment decision due at timestep ``t``?
+
+    ``catch_up=False`` is the historical grid rule: a decision exists only at
+    scheduled epochs, so an epoch whose safety mask admits no cell forfeits its
+    opportunity and, once epochs run out, its token.  ``catch_up=True`` keeps
+    the same authorization schedule but carries an unused authorization
+    forward: a decision is due at every timestep at which fewer tokens have
+    been installed than have accrued, so a token blocked by the hazard mask is
+    installed at the first later timestep with a safe feasible cell.  Every
+    strategy runs on this same rule, which equalizes realized capacity
+    whenever a safe cell exists at all.
+    """
+    if int(deployed) >= int(budget) or int(t) < int(first):
+        return False
+    if bool(catch_up):
+        return int(deployed) < accrued_tokens(
+            t, first=first, interval=interval, budget=budget
+        )
+    return (int(t) - int(first)) % int(interval) == 0
